Can an Abstract Base Class (ABC) in Python contain concrete (implemented) non-abstract methods?
```python
from abc import ABC, abstractmethod

class BaseProcessor(ABC):
    @abstractmethod
    def process(self):
        pass
    def log(self):
        return "Logged"

class TextProcessor(BaseProcessor):
    def process(self):
        return "Processing"

tp = TextProcessor()
print(tp.process(), tp.log())
```

