What is the difference between `__str__` and `__repr__` in the following code?
```python
class Book:
    def __init__(self, title):
        self.title = title
    def __str__(self):
        return f"Book: {self.title}"
    def __repr__(self):
        return f"Book({self.title!r})"

b = Book("Python 101")
print(str(b), repr(b))
```

